This function is a single call that forwards the field lookup to the base `Mesg` class. There is nothing inside it to optimise, and any real speedup would have to come from the lookup code, which is outside this function.

The rewrite only names the arguments as `constexpr` locals, so the behaviour is identical. I don't expect a measurable change in decode time.

I kept the subfield argument explicit on purpose. The default for that parameter is the active subfield, not the main field, so dropping it would change which value is returned.

```cpp
    FIT_UINT32 GetSurfaceInterval(void) const
    {
        constexpr FIT_UINT8 kFieldNum = 4;
        constexpr FIT_UINT8 kArrayIndex = 0;
        return GetFieldUINT32Value(kFieldNum, kArrayIndex, static_cast<FIT_UINT16>(FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD));
    }
```